  <iati-identifier>XM-DAC-7-PPR-260000293</iati-identifier>
  <reporting-org ref="XM-DAC-7" type="10">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ministry of Foreign Affairs of the Netherlands</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening Civ. Soc. Monitoring of the Ogoni Clean-up &amp; Enhancing Transparency and Accountability in Host Community Development Trusts in the Delta</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project strengthens freedom of expression, transparency, and inclusive participation in environmental governance in the Niger Delta, focusing on the Ogoni clean-up and Host Community Development Trusts (HCDTs). Limited access to reliable information and weak community engagement undermine accountability in both remediation and development processes, while women, youth, and marginalized groups remain excluded from decision-making.

The project will build the capacity of civil society and community monitors to conduct independent technical monitoring, generate credible data, and support evidence-based advocacy. It will also promote improved remediation practices through engagement with HYPREP and government institutions, while strengthening HCDT governance through enhanced transparency, communication, and accountability mechanisms.

By improving access to information and supporting inclusive participation, the project enables communities to voice concerns, influence decisions, and hold institutions accountable.</narrative>
  </description>
